417 true] [17592186423588 1069 "q-74112" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423588 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423588 1071 "Given $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖a‖.$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423588 1072 #uuid "203f62af-5fb6-55c0-adc4-39591e34a84e" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423588 1074 "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖a‖ & =\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423589 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423585 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423589 1069 "q-39763" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423589 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423589 1071 "Find the distance between the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $0.$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423589 1072 #uuid "3e3e1b93-57b0-53a0-86f4-45d076c9cfad" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423589 1074 "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,0) & =‖x-0‖ \\\\  & =‖x‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-18)^{2}+(-12)^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+324+144+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{529} \\\\  & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423590 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423579 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423590 1069 "q-39217" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423590 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423590 1071 "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2k\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ k \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find $k$, if the distance between the vectors is $\\text{d}(x,y)=\\sqrt{83}.$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423590 1072 #uuid "48de0343-fd7b-5b5e-947b-c8f60a378766" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423590 1074 "First, we calculate the distance between $x$ and $y$ in terms of $k:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{y}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(k-0)^{2}+(0-k)^{2}+((-1)-(-2))^{2}+(-2k-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{k}^{2}+{k}^{2}+{1}^{2}+4{k}^{2}+8k+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}+8k+5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given equation  $\\text{d}(x,y)=\\sqrt{83},$ we obtain an equation that we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}+8k+5} & =\\sqrt{83} \\\\ {(\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}+8k+5})}^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{83})}^{2} \\\\ 6{k}^{2}+8k+5 & =83 \\\\ 6{k}^{2}+8k-78 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the quadratic formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\pm \\sqrt{{8}^{2}-4(6)(-78)}}{2(6)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\pm \\sqrt{1\\,936}}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\pm 44}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2\\pm 11}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives $k=3$ and $k=-\\frac{13}{3}.$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423591 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423581 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423591 1069 "q-74146" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423591 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423591 1071 "Normalize the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423591 1072 #uuid "6fe81e21-b32f-5653-9746-86ee81aa65aa" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423591 1074 "To normalize a vector $x,$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\frac{x}{‖x‖}.$ Therefore, to normalize $x,$ we first calculate $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+16+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $x$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{-1}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423592 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423584 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423592 1069 "q-74130" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423592 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423592 1071 "Given the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖4v‖.$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423592 1072 #uuid "8cc596a5-8803-52b2-93a7-a243d5af26bc" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423592 1074 "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n‖kv‖=|k|\\cdot ‖v‖\n$$\n\nUsing this fact and the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖4v‖ & =|4|\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{1+9+1+9} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423593 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423586 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423593 1069 "q-74149" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423593 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423593 1071 "Find $k$, if $u=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{k}{4}\\end{aligned}]$ is a unit vector." 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423593 1072 #uuid "9c46599f-15c6-531f-94db-06b03ec04f84" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423593 1074 "First, we calculate the norm of the vector $u$ in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u‖ & =\\sqrt{{u}_{1}^{2}+{u}_{2}^{2}+{u}_{3}^{2}+{u}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}+{(\\frac{k}{4})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{16}+\\frac{9}{16}+\\frac{{k}^{2}}{16}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{14+{k}^{2}}{16}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given equation  $‖u‖=1,$ we obtain an equation that we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{14+{k}^{2}}{16}} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{14+{k}^{2}} & =4 \\\\ {(\\sqrt{14+{k}^{2}})}^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ 14+{k}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =2 \\\\ k & =\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423594 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423580 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423594 1069 "q-74118" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423594 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423594 1071 "Given $w=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖w‖.$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423594 1072 #uuid "a076c01e-29ae-51f5-9ba7-a79f626ba8b5" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423594 1074 "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖w‖ & =\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}+{w}_{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{9}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(\\sqrt{10})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+1+81+4+10} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423595 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423578 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423595 1069 "q-74119" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423595 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423595 1071 "Given $x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖x‖.$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423595 1072 #uuid "a59db3f3-f5cf-55e8-a066-a483320cdf58" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423595 1074 "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}+{x}_{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}+{8}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+9+64+9+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423596 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423577 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423596 1069 "q-39214" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423596 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423596 1071 "Normalize the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423596 1072 #uuid "a75afdb8-44f8-53fc-b291-78342131f3c9" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423596 1074 "To normalize a vector $x,$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\frac{x}{‖x‖}.$ Therefore, to normalize $x,$ we first calculate $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $x$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423597 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423576 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423597 1069 "q-74123" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423597 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423597 1071 "Given the vectors $a=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$, find the distance $\\text{d}(a,b).$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423597 1072 #uuid "cbc4c264-a470-51c7-b34c-2fec35b37aa8" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423597 1074 "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(a,b) & =‖a-b‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({a}_{1}-{b}_{1})^{2}+({a}_{2}-{b}_{2})^{2}+({a}_{3}-{b}_{3})^{2}+({a}_{4}-{b}_{4})^{2}+({a}_{5}-{b}_{5})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(5-3)^{2}+(3-5)^{2}+(-1-1)^{2}+(1-(-1))^{2}+(6-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4+4+4+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423598 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423573 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423598 1069 "q-39245" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423598 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423598 1071 "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2k \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ Find $k$, if $‖x‖=3\\sqrt{6}.$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423598 1072 #uuid "d68ac222-1a16-5cb9-b7e0-2d9347a41d3b" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423598 1074 "First, we calculate the norm of the vector $x$ in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(2k)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4{k}^{2}+25+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{k}^{2}+38}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given equation  $‖x‖=3\\sqrt{6},$ we obtain an equation that we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{4{k}^{2}+38} & =3\\sqrt{6} \\\\ {(\\sqrt{4{k}^{2}+38})}^{2} & ={(3\\sqrt{6})}^{2} \\\\ 4{k}^{2}+38 & =9\\cdot 6 \\\\ 4{k}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =4 \\\\ k & =\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423599 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423575 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423599 1069 "q-74115" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423599 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423599 1071 "Given $e=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖e‖.$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423599 1072 #uuid "e0a1770e-420b-5cd7-b796-0a2eb2b938da" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423599 1074 "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖e‖ & =\\sqrt{{e}_{1}^{2}+{e}_{2}^{2}+{e}_{3}^{2}+{e}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+1+9+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{39}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423600 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423582 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423600 1069 "q-74132" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423600 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423600 1071 "If $‖-2x‖=3$, find $‖6x‖.$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423600 1072 #uuid "eca368ca-a4ba-5312-b178-c63c0431130b" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true] [17592186423600 1074 "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n‖kx‖=|k|\\cdot ‖x‖\n$$\n\nUsing this fact, we can solve for the norm $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-2x‖ & =3 \\\\ |-2|\\cdot ‖x‖ & =3 \\\\ ‖x‖ & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $‖6x‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖6x‖ & =6\\cdot ‖x‖ \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534508 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0301abe0-3c1d-5d0f-ba9c-e0b6f7e434e4" 17592186423503 "answer-0321dad9-7a91-5b43-b252-10b7425bf47e" 17592186423504 "answer-04dbab12-ca8b-5d27-a241-6617b3607e24" 17592186423505 "answer-06a5fc03-9e34-57fb-8e35-1287e254f707" 17592186423506 "answer-09cd35ab-5375-5955-b3eb-b86578cb2956" 17592186423507 "answer-0b0ef00b-610f-581a-8e67-24f68a95faf0" 17